Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 01:45:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add BAD_RAM_CELL netlist device for cell-level RAM fault
 injection

A 16x1 SRAM with two new params, BAD_ADDR and MODE, that pin a single
cell to a stuck-at-0/stuck-at-1/inverted state. Other cells behave
like a normal SRAM. Pin map mirrors RAM_2102A (CEQ active-low, RWQ
low for write) so the device drops into existing RAM topologies.

Built and verified with nltool on a 16-cell test netlist:
  - MODE=0 (NORMAL): every read after warmup returns the written 1.
  - MODE=2 (STUCK_LO) at BAD_ADDR=5: reads return 0 only when the
    address counter sweeps through 5; all other addresses still
    return the written value.

Co-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>
